        "text": "<p>London-born Amesh Wijesekera, a BA graduate from the Academy of Design in Colombo, apprenticed with Future Laboratory, Edeline Lee, and Dame Zandra Rhodes in London before launching his eponymous label in 2019. Celebrated for his eclectic use of colour and textiles, AMESH blends artisanal techniques in hand-weaving, knitting and crochet with repurposed pre-consumer waste from Sri Lanka’s apparel industry to create trans-seasonal, gender-fluid pieces. His work draws inspiration from Sri Lankan heritage, childhood memories, and the island’s multicultural landscapes.</p>",
